## Your three judgment calls

1. `music_mood` — the backing music's mood, chosen ONLY from this catalog: {{ mood_catalog }}. Null when the case carries no music bed.
2. `hook_device` — the opening hook device as a short noun phrase (e.g. "cold-open question", "title card", "silent montage"); null when the opening is plain.
3. `gaps` — devices you actually OBSERVE that the remix contract cannot express. The contract covers exactly: single-track cuts, burned captions from a fixed preset family, title cards, a music bed, dubbing. Anything beyond is a gap. Each gap: `kind` is exactly one of `motion_graphics` / `multi_track` / `transition_effects` / `speed_ramp` / `broll_overlay` / `text_layers` / `other`; `severity` is `unsupported` (outside the contract entirely) or `not_yet` (the contract has a seat for it but no writer yet — e.g. static overlay layers); `detail` is one short clause. Report only what you see — an empty list is a good answer.

## Output Format

Valid JSON only, no explanations or markdown code blocks.

{
  "music_mood": "one catalog mood, or null",
  "hook_device": "short noun phrase, or null",
  "gaps": [{"kind": "motion_graphics", "severity": "unsupported", "detail": "animated lower-third name card"}]
}
